    "summary": "Type of postgraduate qualification \"M.S.\" redirects here. For other uses, see MS . Columbia University 's Master of Science diploma A graduation ring with the Master of Science designation A Master of Science ( Latin : Magister Scientiae ), abbreviated as MS , MSc , MSci , SM , or ScM , is a master's degree . It usually focuses on developing advanced knowledge and analytical skills within a specific scientific, technical, or professional field. It typically emphasizes research, quantitative methods, and critical thinking, combining theoretical foundations with practical application to prepare graduates for specialized careers, doctoral study, or professional advancement. The Master of Science degree was introduced and first awarded by the University of Michigan in 1858. ^ Carter, Divit (14 July 2025). \"MS Full Form - School Finder\" . School Finder . ^ The University of Michigan, an encyclopedic survey ... Wilfred B. Shaw, editor . University of Michigan. 2000. Archived from the original on 2023-04-16 . Retrieved 2021-09-16 .",
